"Submit a second form (this side only) for alternate signers attached to this form and the argument.","x":333,"y":2903,"w":1867,"h":44}]},{"page":3,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"ARGUMENT AGAINST MEASURE","x":853,"y":342,"w":691,"h":36},{"text":"7","x":1474,"y":451,"w":51,"h":55},{"text":"The Redwood City Council voted 6-0 to oppose Measure","x":297,"y":457,"w":1099,"h":49},{"text":"Me.asure _ was not prepared by the City Council or City staff. The measure repeals strong","x":298,"y":572,"w":1773,"h":47},{"text":"tenant protection measures adopted by the Redwood City Council that exceed State laws","x":296,"y":631,"w":1827,"h":48},{"text":"protecting renters.","x":297,"y":689,"w":348,"h":42},{"text":"Redwood City is committed to protecting renters. Many of us are renters ourselves, and our","x":297,"y":804,"w":1849,"h":47},{"text":"families have lived with the instability this measure claims to address.","x":293,"y":862,"w":1341,"h":45},{"text":"But good intentions don't guarantee good policy. If approved by voters, Measure _ will","x":295,"y":981,"w":1742,"h":47},{"text":"mean less affordable housing, higher prices for renters, and new costs to the City likely","x":294,"y":1039,"w":1682,"h":47},{"text":"impacting essential city programs and services.","x":294,"y":1097,"w":913,"h":44},{"text":"An independent, City-commissioned analysis found this measure would cost Redwood City","x":291,"y":1213,"w":1823,"h":49},{"text":"up to $11 million per year and require up to 18 new full-time employees to administer. The","x":293,"y":1270,"w":1858,"h":48},{"text":"initiative prohibits the City from using General Fund dollars, but the math does not work.","x":292,"y":1330,"w":1698,"h":44},{"text":"Cuts to critical neighborhood services or new taxes will be needed to fund ongoing","x":292,"y":1445,"w":1732,"h":47},{"text":"implementation. Whatis worse, this initiative targets non-profit affordable housing projects,","x":291,"y":1504,"w":1776,"h":47},{"text":"single-family homes and in-law units with onerous regulations and fees.","x":289,"y":1562,"w":1382,"h":45},{"text":"Nonprofit housing providers would face new fees, unsustainable rent restrictions, and","x":291,"y":1679,"w":1793,"h":44},{"text":"tightening operating budgets. This will drain funds needed for repairs, resident services, and","x":287,"y":1736,"w":1835,"h":46},{"text":"long-term preservation of the affordable housing this measure claims to protect.","x":289,"y":1795,"w":1537,"h":46},{"text":"As a citizens' initiative, any future changes to the ordinance will require a costly city-wide","x":285,"y":1911,"w":1827,"h":47},{"text":"election.","x":286,"y":1969,"w":175,"h":34},{"text":"is a housing leader: creating housing near transit, strong Tenant Protections, and","x":575,"y":2088,"w":1561,"h":43},{"text":"millions awarded every year towards affordable housing.","x":286,"y":2144,"w":1093,"h":45},{"text":"This initiative undo our progress, put the City at financial risk, reduce housing choice","x":285,"y":2260,"w":1865,"h":45},{"text":"and affordabäkäty, target homeowners, and halt future affordable housing projects in our","x":285,"y":2319,"w":1822,"h":45},{"text":"communityø","x":285,"y":2377,"w":240,"h":42},{"text":"Redwood City cannot afford Measure","x":285,"y":2493,"w":722,"h":43},{"text":"Vote NO on Measure","x":282,"y":2609,"w":410,"h":35},{"text":"AUG 1 1 2026","x":1372,"y":2713,"w":261,"h":50},{"text":"CITY OF REDWOOD CITY","x":1219,"y":2815,"w":562,"h":58},{"text":"CITY CLERK'S OFFICE","x":1248,"y":2874,"w":498,"h":54},{"text":"II","x":2191,"y":630,"w":27,"h":45},{"text":"17","x":2197,"y":1274,"w":61,"h":51},{"text":"13","x":2199,"y":1742,"w":60,"h":46},{"text":"(3","x":2213,"y":2075,"w":54,"h":43},{"text":"4","x":2221,"y":2467,"w":48,"h":73},{"text":"77","x":2185,"y":2792,"w":121,"h":78}]}]}
